  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "subject-n",
      "topic-n",
      "theme-n"
    ],
    "note": "**Subject** and **topic** both mean what is talked or written about; **topic** is often used for one particular matter within a larger subject (*the topics in this chapter*). A **theme** is the main idea that runs through a book, a film, or a piece of music (*the theme of love*). Only **subject** is used for what you study at school (*my favorite subject*)."
